Click Launch Instance and enter instance name.


Select Ubuntu or Windows AMI and choose t2.micro.


Create and download key pair file (.pem).


Configure Security Group and allow SSH or RDP access.


Launch the EC2 instance successfully.


Connect to Linux instance using SSH, PuTTY, or CloudShell.


Connect to Windows instance using Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP).


Result
Successfully created and connected Linux and Windows EC2 instances.

